.\" Adapted for BNU from the GNU Coreutils 9.11 manual page; see doc/README.md.
.TH CAT "1" "2026-07-28" "BNU 9.11" "BNU Commands"
.SH NAME
cat \- concatenate files and print on the standard output
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cat
[\fI\,OPTION\/\fR]... [\fI\,FILE\/\fR]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.\" This page is derived from GNU Coreutils documentation.
This page documents BNU, an independent Bun implementation compatible with
GNU Coreutils 9.11.
.PP
Concatenate FILE(s) to standard output.
.PP
With no FILE, or when FILE is \-, read standard input.
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cat-A'\fB\-A, \-\-show\-all\fP\X'tty: link'
equivalent to \fB\-vET\fR
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cat-b'\fB\-b, \-\-number\-nonblank\fP\X'tty: link'
number nonempty output lines, overrides \fB\-n\fR
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cat-e'\fB\-e\fP\X'tty: link'
equivalent to \fB\-vE\fR
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cat-E'\fB\-E, \-\-show\-ends\fP\X'tty: link'
display $ or ^M$ at end of each line
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cat-n'\fB\-n, \-\-number\fP\X'tty: link'
number all output lines
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cat-s'\fB\-s, \-\-squeeze\-blank\fP\X'tty: link'
suppress repeated empty output lines
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cat-t'\fB\-t\fP\X'tty: link'
equivalent to \fB\-vT\fR
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cat-T'\fB\-T, \-\-show\-tabs\fP\X'tty: link'
display TAB characters as ^I
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cat-u'\fB\-u\fP\X'tty: link'
(ignored)
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/manual/coreutils.html#cat-v'\fB\-v, \-\-show\-nonprinting\fP\X'tty: link'
use ^ and M\- notation, except for LFD and TAB
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/cat#cat--help'\fB\-\-help\fP\X'tty: link'
display this help and exit
.TP
\X'tty: link https://www.gnu.org/software/coreutils/cat#cat--version'\fB\-\-version\fP\X'tty: link'
output version information and exit
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
cat f \- g
Output f's contents, then standard input, then g's contents.
.TP
cat
Copy standard input to standard output.
